\import{discrete-macros}

\p{In fact, the way the [rules for proof](0057) were presented is (mostly) constructive logic!  Rather than defining each connective by a truth table, we can actually \em{define} each connective by its introduction and elimination rules, \ie by how to prove them, and how to use them if we already know them.}

